🚽 Test case: `!` yields cap, and cap does not become rizz implicitly.
🚽
🚽 C would allow `int k = !n;`. Brainrot already refuses `rizz k = W;` and
🚽 arithmetic on a cap, so refusing this is the existing design being
🚽 consistent rather than a gap in the operator. Recorded as a fixture so
🚽 the choice is deliberate and cannot drift silently.
skibidi main {
    rizz n = 5;
    rizz k = !n;
    yapping("%d", k);
    bussin 0;
}
